{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBxom5ge1T5J1hTgGMPN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A new allergy goes from the form workspace through `saveAllergy` in `allergy-form.resource.ts`, a `POST` to `/patient/{uuid}/allergy`. The REST resource `PatientAllergyResource2_0.save` hands it to `PatientService.saveAllergy`, which calls `PatientDAO.saveAllergy`, and Hibernate persists it.\n\n1. **Frontend request:** `onSubmit` in `allergy-form.workspace.tsx` builds the payload with `createAllergyPayload` and calls `saveAllergy` when not editing (`updatePatientAllergy` when editing). `saveAllergy` in `allergy-form.resource.ts` posts the payload to `${restBaseUrl}/patient/${patientUuid}/allergy` via `openmrsFetch`.\n2. **REST handler:** `PatientAllergyResource2_0.save` links each reaction to the new allergy, calls `Context.getPatientService().saveAllergy(newAllergy)`, then re-reads it by UUID to return it.\n3. **Core service:** `PatientServiceImpl.saveAllergy` delegates straight to `dao.saveAllergy`. The interface method in `PatientService` carries an `@PreAuthorize` check for the add-allergies privilege.\n4. **Data access:** `HibernatePatientDAO.saveAllergy` calls `sessionFactory.getCurrentSession().persist(allergy)`. The interface is `PatientDAO.saveAllergy`.\n\nTwo things I did not verify: the REST controller that routes `POST /patient/{uuid}/allergy` to the resource (I cited the resource's `save` as the handler), and where `AllergyValidator` is invoked on save. There is also a second frontend `saveAllergy` in `allergy-intolerance.resource.ts` (line 54), which I list for recall but which the form does not use.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-allergies-app/src/allergies/allergies-form/allergy-form.resource.ts\", \"startLine\": 136, \"endLine\": 145},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-allergies-app/src/allergies/allergies-form/all